  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f69c6b1f1e1fc2c4b9a85c7696ada520, type: 3}
  m_Name: AfterCasino4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogSO
  replics:
  - 'Cyber. Hi. '
  - "I don\u2019t talk to peasants."
  - "Yeah, yeah. I remember. But right now let\u2019s talk as if I\u2019m not your
    sister, you\u2019re not my brother, and we\u2019ve put all personal matters aside.
    I have a very profitable offer for you."
  - A profitable offer? Returning my budget, perhaps?
  - "That too, actually. So listen \u2014 I want freedom. I want to leave the country.
    You want to go home, back to your family."
  - Alright. I admit that sounds slightly more interesting now.
  - "Asahi and I were discussing escape plans, you understand? At the rate we\u2019re
    going, the debt will never disappear."
  - Every time it gets smaller, they cut our budget so the debt increases again from
    food purchases and personal expenses. Sometimes they just randomly add fines
    too.
  - Get to the point.
  - "As long as you\u2019re here, they\u2019ll never connect you to a proper lawyer.
    We need you to hack the entire security system \u2014 but not all at once."
  - "ver the course of a month, you need to gradually push it toward total failure
    so that when everything collapses, they notice the \u201Ctechnical malfunctions\u201D
    first instead of our breach."
  - It has to look like a chain reaction caused by failing infrastructure across
    the whole system.
  - 'And what exactly do I get in return? '
  - "You leave with us. We guarantee your safety until you reach the lawyer. He\u2019ll
    reconnect you with your family immediately. And your family can simply buy you
    out."
  - "Hm\u2026 so without this, you\u2019re saying I have no chance?"
  - None.
  - And how will you prove that?
  - "We\u2019re all meeting in the conference room tonight. We\u2019ll discuss the
    details there. You\u2019ll get your proof too."
